nd with keyboard\n  input only, Then every step completes successfully with no focus traps and no\n  unreachable controls — measured by a keyboard-only walkthrough of the flow.\n- Given the workbench spawn flow, When operated end to end with keyboard input\n  only, Then every step completes with no focus traps and no unreachable\n  controls — measured by a keyboard-only walkthrough of the flow.\n- Given the model deployment flow, When operated end to end with keyboard input\n  only, Then every step completes with no focus traps and no unreachable\n  controls — measured by a keyboard-only walkthrough of the flow.\n- Given the pipeline run submission flow, When operated end to end with keyboard\n  input only, Then every step completes with no focus traps and no unreachable\n  controls — measured by a keyboard-only walkthrough of the flow.\n- Every defect enumerated in the audit report for the four audited flows is\n  remediated in code, or explicitly dispositioned with rationale.\n- Focus indicators are visible on all interactive controls in the audited flows\n  and use a consistent style — measured by inspection across the four flows.\n- Automated accessibility checks covering keyboard and focus rules pass on the\n  audited flows with no new violations introduced — measured by the check run\n  on the changed builds.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P1)**: The four audited core flows are fully operable by keyboard,\n  with no focus traps or unreachable controls — covered by the keyboard\n  remediation of the four flows in this epic.\n- **HLR-2 (P1)**: Visible focus indicators are consistent across the audited\n  flows — covered by the consistent focus-indicator work in this epic; kept in\n  the same epic as HLR-1 because both concern the same flows, component, and\n  team, and a split would audit the same surfaces twice.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":26839,"output_tokens":0},"context_management