{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83c9855922853253","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9017-E001\n3\ttitle: Keyboard accessibility remediation for the four audited Dashboard flows\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9017\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Keyboard accessibility remediation for the four audited Dashboard flows\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic remediates the keyboard accessibility defects identified by the\n34\taccessibility audit in the four core Dashboard flows: project creation, workbench\n35\tspawn, model deployment, and pipeline run submission. On completion, each of the\n36\tfour flows is fully operable with keyboard alone — focus is managed correctly in\n37\tmodals, no control is unreachable, and focus indicators are consistent. This is\n38\tthe code deliverable of the keyboard accessibility conformance strategy and the\n39\tfoundation for the updated conformance documentation.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Remediate every defect enumerated in the accessibility audit report for the\n44\t  four audited flows (project creation, workbench spawn, model deployment,\n45\t  pipeline run submission), including focus loss in modals and unreachable\n46\t  controls.\n47\t- Implement correct focus management in modals and dialogs used by the audited\n48\t  flows: focus moves into the modal on open, is trapped while open, returns to\n49\t  the triggering control on close, and standard dismiss keys work.\n50\t- Make every interactive control in the audited flows reachable and operable by\n51\t  keyboard alone.\n52\t- Apply a consistent, visible focus indicator style across all interactive\n53\t  controls in the audited flows.\n54\t- Verify the fixes do not regress non-audited behavior of the affected\n55\t  components.\n56\t- Out of scope: screen-reader semantics beyond what the keyboard fixes require,\n57\t  and flows outside the four audited ones.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- Given the project creation flow, When it is operated end to end with keyboard\n62\t  input only, Then every step completes successfully with no focus traps and no\n63\t  unreachable controls — measured by a keyboard-only walkthrough of the flow.\n64\t- Given the workbench spawn flow, When operated end to end with keyboard input\n65\t  only, Then every step completes with no focus traps and no unreachable\n66\t  controls — measured by a keyboard-only walkthrough of the flow.\n67\t- Given the model deployment flow, When operated end to end with keyboard input\n68\t  only, Then every step completes with no focus traps and no unreachable\n69\t  controls — measured by a keyboard-only walkthrough of the flow.\n70\t- Given the pipeline run submission flow, When operated end to end with keyboard\n71\t  input only, Then every step completes with no focus traps and no unreachable\n72\t  controls — measured by a keyboard-only walkthrough of the flow.\n73\t- Every defect enumerated in the audit report for the four audited flows is\n74\t  remediated in code, or explicitly dispositioned with rationale.\n75\t- Focus indicators are visible on all interactive controls in the audited flows\n76\t  and use a consistent style — measured by inspection across the four flows.\n77\t- Automated accessibility checks covering keyboard and focus rules pass on the\n78\t  audited flows with no new violations introduced — measured by the check run\n79\t  on the changed builds.\n80\t\n81\t## HLR Traceability\n82\t\n83\t- **HLR-1 (P1)**: The four audited core flows are fully operable by keyboard,\n84\t  with no focus traps or unreachable controls — covered by the keyboard\n85\t  remediation of the four flows in this epic.\n86\t- **HLR-2 (P1)**: Visible focus indicators are consistent across the audited\n87\t  flows — covered by the consistent focus-indicator work in this epic; kept in\n88\t  the same epic as HLR-1 because both concern the same flows, component, and\n89\t  team, and a split would audit the same surfaces twice.\n90\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2a412fcc8a4d7c3","agent_id":"a7a602bd4af061252","session_id":"d2f07c2f-aad3-43e7-a558-783e1249f639","uuid":"af3d95da-50f8-42b1-a2a2-f0d2b931c57c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:30:18.103Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-83c9855922853253","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9017 decomposition"}
