{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b952c0caa6c4bcc0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9017\n3\tscore: 14\n4\tpass: true\n5\trecommendation: accept\n6\tissues: []\n7\terror: null\n8\t---\n9\t## Review Summary\n10\t\n11\tScore: 14/14 — pass\n12\tRecommendation: accept\n13\t\n14\tcontract validator: OK (exit 0 — epic body sections, canonical component names, Rule 11\n15\tdocs-last coverage, priority inheritance, and implementation-type parallelism all pass;\n16\tthis review graded only what the script cannot check).\n17\t\n18\tTriage consistency: `triage: null` (full decomposition) with `epic_count: 2` — consistent;\n19\tmulti-epic output is expected for a full decomposition and is not penalized.\n20\t\n21\t## Criterion Details\n22\t\n23\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n24\tAll three HLRs are mapped and traceable: HLR-1 (P1) and HLR-2 (P1) → E001, HLR-3 (P2) →\n25\tE002. The traceability matrix is present in the decomposition summary and each epic's\n26\tHLR Traceability section restates its coverage. No P0 HLRs exist in this strategy, so the\n27\tP0-inheritance rule is trivially satisfied; E001 carries P1, matching its P1 HLRs. E002 is\n28\ta `docs-authoring` epic at P2 (strategy priority Normal → P2) — the docs-authoring\n29\tpriority exception applies and its Rule 11 dependency on the P1 E001 is correctly not\n30\tflagged as a priority inheritance violation. No priority collapse: HLR-1 and HLR-2 are\n31\tboth P1 and share the same implementation surface (same flows, component, team), so\n32\tbundling them in E001 is correct, and the bundling rationale is recorded in the matrix row.\n33\t\n34\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n35\tSingle edge E001 → E002, justified by Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by all Implementation\n36\tepics) — a valid edge that does not trigger priority inheritance. Frontmatter dependencies\n37\t(E001: [], E002: [RHAISTRAT-9017-E001]) exactly match the summary DAG diagram, and the\n38\tdiagram arrow direction follows the dependency→dependent convention. No cycles, no invalid\n39\tedges, no missing data/artifact dependencies (the only cross-epic coupling — docs\n40\tdescribing the fixed state — is the Rule 11 edge itself). No konflux-onboarding,\n41\trepo-onboarding, or license-validation epics exist, so Rules 7/8/10 parallelism is not in\n42\tplay. No conditional branch files. Critical path length 2 is appropriate for a small\n43\tstrategy (S heuristic: 1-2).\n44\t\n45\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n46\tThe two epics split precisely along the component/team tuple boundary: E001\n47\t(Dashboard / RHOAI Dashboard) and E002 (Documentation / RHOAI Documentation). E001 is one\n48\tlogical change — the audit-enumerated keyboard remediation across four flows in one\n49\tcomponent with one team and one change type — so a single epic is the correct shape, and\n50\tit does not clearly exceed the ~2-week guideline. No scope duplication between epics, no\n51\twork-product type mixing (code remediation and content authoring are correctly separated),\n52\tand no standalone enforcement epic. The inferred team assignments are flagged as a Health\n53\tWarning with human verification recommended, which is the right handling given the strategy\n54\tnames no teams.\n55\t\n56\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n57\tBoth epics are typed Implementation, which is correct: E001 produces code changes and E002\n58\tproduces published documents (correctly subtyped `implementation_type: docs-authoring`).\n59\tNo Investigation epics are needed — the strategy explicitly states there are no open\n60\tquestions and the audit enumerates the exact defects per flow, so there is no uncertainty\n61\tthat would change downstream structure. No `gated_by`/`gate_failure_impact` fields are set,\n62\tand none are required.\n63\t\n64\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n65\tBoth epics are Implementation type and correctly carry `ai_signals` (9-signal rubric) with\n66\t`investigation_signals: null`. Signal values are consistent with the rationales in the\n67\tai-signals files and with the strategy content. Calibration spot-checks against\n68\t`.context`: E001's `architecture_claims: 1` is corroborated — the rationale cites\n69\t`architecture/rhoai-3.0/dashboard.md`, which does describe the Dashboard as the GA\n70\tsingle-pane web console surfacing projects, workbenches, model serving, and pipelines.\n71\tE002's `architecture_claims: 0` is also accurate — no architecture-context file covers the\n72\tDocumentation component. E002's `human_process_gates: -1` correctly reflects the\n73\tHLR-3-mandated technical review, and `repo_access: 0` honestly reflects the unidentified\n74\tdocs repository. Per instructions, computed `ai_implementability`/`ai_implementability_score`\n75\tvalues were not checked.\n76\t\n77\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n78\tE001 has seven testable ACs — one keyboard-only walkthrough per audited flow (all four\n79\tnamed flows covered), full audit-defect remediation-or-disposition, consistent focus\n80\tindicators by inspection, and automated accessibility checks with no new violations. E002\n81\thas the rule-mandated technical-review AC (\"a reviewer confirms each conformance claim…\n82\tmeasured by a completed review sign-off\") plus republish and claim-scoping ACs. No\n83\treplacement epic exists, so no rollback/feature-flag AC is required; no konflux chain, so\n84\tno build-pipeline AC applies. No AC states an externally-controlled precondition — the\n85\treview sign-off AC is measured on the epic's own deliverable (the recorded review), not on\n86\ta third party's schedule. No epic body references sibling epics by draft ID.\n87\t\n88\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n89\tThe full strategy scope is accounted for: all four audited flows (project creation,\n90\tworkbench spawn, model deployment, pipeline run submission) in E001's scope and ACs;\n91\tfocus-indicator consistency (HLR-2) in E001; VPAT update, accessibility statement update,\n92\trepublish, and technical review (HLR-3) in E002. Out-of-scope boundaries (screen-reader\n93\tsemantics beyond the keyboard fixes, non-audited flows) are respected and — a good catch —\n94\texplicitly enforced by E002's claim-scoping AC so the conformance documentation cannot\n95\tover-claim. Strategy-level context is carried forward: the public-sector renewal pressure\n96\tappears in E002's description and as a priority observation in Health Warnings; missing\n97\tstrategy sections are recorded as non-blocking Health Warnings. A `docs-authoring` epic\n98\texists for the documentation deliverable (Rule 11 satisfied).\n99\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9480ebde80f856b8","agent_id":"a190d143d9ae09037","session_id":"d2f07c2f-aad3-43e7-a558-783e1249f639","uuid":"74612613-277f-46c9-ac6c-f438263476a7","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:32:22.820Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b952c0caa6c4bcc0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9017 decomposition"}
